 """
 strategy/volatility_regime.py
-Volatility regime detection — no options feed required.
-
-Uses SPY 10-day realized volatility (annualized) as a VIX proxy.
-Classifies market into three regimes and returns size/stop multipliers.
-
-Regimes:
-  LOW_VOL    (<12% annualized) — low-vol grind, trends are clean, size up
-  NORMAL     (12–25%)          — baseline behavior
-  HIGH_VOL   (>25%)            — panic/expansion, chop increases, size down
+Volatility regime detection.
+
+VIX (REGIME-SIZE-1104, owner direction 2026-11-04: "the actual box reading, not some composite reading"):
+  the CBOE $VIX index itself, with its own as-of time, from (1) the owner's Schwab market-data feed
+  ($VIX, every call), else (2) the T4 yfinance ^VIX chart (as-of = regularMarketTime). SPY realized
+  volatility is NEVER used as VIX; it is reported separately as `spy_rvol_10d`.
+  [FMP ^VIX (T2) is the planned middle tier; it needs a quote function in the FMP client module.]
+
+Result fields:
+  vix_value / vix_source / vix_as_of / vix_age_s / vix_fresh - the highest-tier VIX whose own as-of
+      time is within 2 scan intervals of now (vix_source "none" when there is none; then VIX rules
+      are not applied).
+  vix_basis_value / vix_basis_source / vix_basis_as_of - the most recent real VIX reading from any
+      tier or earlier in this process, whatever its age (for stop width: a missing feed must not
+      narrow a stop).
+  realized_vol - kept for existing callers: the basis VIX value, 0.0 when no VIX was ever read
+      (callers already treat 0.0 as "no reading").
+  spy_rvol_10d - SPY 10-day realized vol, annualized %, a separate series (T1 Alpaca bars).
+
+Regimes: HIGH_VOL (VIX > REGIME_HIGH_VOL_THRESHOLD; from the fresh VIX, or from the basis when no
+fresh VIX exists — a stale reading may only tighten), LOW_VOL (FRESH VIX < REGIME_LOW_VOL_THRESHOLD; a
+label the capital allocator reads, with NO size-up), else NORMAL.
+The low-vol 1.25x "size up" and the unread stop multiplier were removed: no regime multiplier above
+1.0 exists, and the core-tier share count is set by the value cap in the entry sizing path.
 
 Composite regime (display-only, no effect on sizing):
-  BULL       — SPY > 50d SMA AND VIX/VIX3M < 1.0 AND 20d rvol < 25%
-  BEAR       — SPY < 50d SMA AND VIX/VIX3M > 1.0 AND 20d rvol > 30%
-  HIGH_VOL   — VIX/VIX3M > 1.1 (inverted term structure, regardless of direction)
-  NEUTRAL    — everything else
+  BULL       - SPY > 50d SMA AND VIX/VIX3M < 1.0 AND 20d rvol < 25%
+  BEAR       - SPY < 50d SMA AND VIX/VIX3M > 1.0 AND 20d rvol > 30%
+  HIGH_VOL   - VIX/VIX3M > 1.1 (inverted term structure, regardless of direction)
+  NEUTRAL    - everything else
   VIX3M failures: single = debug log + default NORMAL; 3+ consecutive = WARNING log.
 """
 
